      "body": "## Purpose\r\nThis PR fixes a critical `TypeError` when running `vllm bench serve`. \r\n\r\nThe upstream benchmark runner invokes the `sample` method by passing the `tokenizer` as a positional argument. However, the overridden `sample` method inside the `SpecBench` class in `vllm/benchmarks/datasets/datasets.py` was incorrectly defined with a single asterisk pointer (`*kwargs`). This forced Python to interpret it as a positional tuple aggregator rather than keyword arguments, making it unable to accept the positional `tokenizer`.\r\n\r\nThis fix corrects the method signature by adding `self`, `*args`, and `**kwargs` to the `SpecBench.sample` definition, ensuring that the positional `tokenizer` argument is properly captured and forwarded to `super().sample()`.\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\nExecute the benchmark server client targeting the `spec_bench` dataset with the following command:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nvllm bench serve \\\r\n   --host 100.100.135.178 \\\r\n   --port 8178 \\\r\n   --model qwen3-8B \\\r\n   --tokenizer /data/Qwen3-8B \\\r\n   --dataset-name spec_bench \\\r\n   --dataset-path /*/N-gram/SpecEval/datasets/spec_bench/question.jsonl \\\r\n   --num-prompts 1000 \\\r\n   --request-rate 20 \\\r\n   --custom-output-len 512 \\\r\n   --save-result \\\r\n   --compilation-config '{\"cudagraph_mode\": \"FULL_DECODE_ONLY\"}' \\\r\n   --save-detailed",
      "changedFiles": 1,
      "comments": {
