  "inline_comments": [
    {
      "body": "![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)\n\nThe addition of `*args` to the method signature is incomplete because these arguments are not passed to the parent class. On line 2537, the call is `super().sample(**kwargs)`, which drops any positional arguments captured in `*args`.\n\nSince the PR's goal is to support the `tokenizer` being passed as a positional argument, this implementation will still result in a `TypeError` inside `super().sample()` because required arguments (like `tokenizer` and `num_requests`) will be missing from `kwargs` if they were passed positionally to `SpecBench.sample`.\n\nTo fix this, you should update the call to `super().sample(*args, **kwargs)`. Alternatively, since `SpecBench.sample` does not add any custom logic, you could consider removing this override entirely and inheriting the `sample` method from `CustomDataset` directly.",
      "created_at": "2026-05-22T10:36:41Z",
      "diff_hunk": "@@ -2529,6 +2529,7 @@ def load_data(self) -> None:\n \n     def sample(\n         self,\n+        *args,",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/43418#discussion_r3287756335",
      "id": 3287756335,
